# None of these affect the module hash; excluding them keeps the build context
# small and the in-container build path clean. The dfx metadata embeds no git
# rev or timestamp (only pinned tool versions), so omitting .git is safe.
#
# The cost of omitting .git is that the container cannot tell a clean checkout
# from a working tree with local edits, and cannot record which commit it
# built. tools/reproducible-build.sh covers both from outside: it refuses a
# dirty tree and passes the HEAD commit in as SOURCE_COMMIT. Build through the
# script, not `docker build` directly, or the artifact is bound to no commit.
target
.dfx
node_modules
.git
